# Kingdom of Kroz II (Apogee, 1990; freeware): installed from its own
# archive with its DEICE inside DOS, then played. tests/keys.py turns this
# into the runners' --key options. The machine: an IBM XT with IBM's BIOS,
# 640 KB (256 on the motherboard and a memory card), CGA, the XT-IDE card
# with the XTIDE Universal BIOS the core carries, and a 10 MB hard disk the
# gate makes: FreeDOS, and the game's archive in C:\KRZINST. FreeDOS's
# prompt is there by frame 7000.
7000 type cd krzinst\n
7200 type install\n
# DEICE: "Which drive to install to?" C; "Enter directory name to copy
# into:" \KROZ as offered; "That directory does not exist! Create it?" Y.
# Then PKSFX unpacks KINGDOM.EXE and the batch file deletes the archive:
# C:\KROZ> by frame 13000.
8100 type c
8500 key Enter 4
8700 type y
13000 type kingdom\n
# "Is your screen Color or Monochrome (C/M)?" C; "Slow or Fast PC (S/F)?"
# S (an XT); the title, a key; "Novice, Experienced or Advanced?" N; the
# instructions, a key; the registration notice, a key; the menu, B (begin
# your descent).
14000 type c
14400 type s
15000 key Space 4
15500 type n
15900 key Space 4
16600 key Space 4
17200 type b
# level 1: "Press any key to begin this level", then four steps right and
# two up (the player moves; some steps meet a wall)
18200 key Space 4
